  "compiled_findings": [
    "Each class gained exactly one method body and exactly one instance trait, the one its source adds (beginDeferredLocalHost; refreshStatus; the label setter). No method or trait was removed. Body counts 91->92, 16->17, 8->9.",
    "With every operand resolved to text and branches to instruction ordinals, and with the two compiler spellings below folded, the only pre-existing methods whose compiled form differs are the ones whose source was edited: LobbyController onChangeReadyStateHandle, onStartMatchHandle, onCampaignHostReady; LocalMatchControls onProtocolFrame; none in LocalCreateRoomOption. beginCampaignLocalHost and isProductionLocalRoom (the production protocol 3 path) are in the unchanged set of that comparison.",
    "FINDING, not explained by the source difference: 35 LobbyController methods and 8 LocalMatchControls methods whose source is unchanged were stored with different instructions. Two spellings account for all of them: (a) an explicit conversion Boolean(x)/String(x)/int(x)/uint(x)/Number(x) was `x; convert_*` (String: coerce_s) and is now `findpropstrict T; x; callproperty T,1`; (b) a builtin member such as indexOf/splice/push/test/toFixed was the QName in the AS3 namespace and is now a late-bound multiname whose open namespace set contains that namespace. So the three tags were compiled by a different compiler build or configuration than the predecessor tags; the commit does not record which.",
    "Those two spellings are treated as the same statement by this comparison, not proved equivalent by it. Known difference of (a) for String: the old coerce_s kept a null operand null, the new call yields the text \"null\"; the new form is the literal meaning of the source `String(x)`. Whether a null can reach such a conversion in the affected methods was not analysed.",
    "The strict (unfolded) and folded method deltas of all three classes are in classes[].resolved_delta; composition.verify recomputes them from the preserved predecessor tags and the tree tags and refuses a mismatch."
  ],
  "source_findings": [
    "The source difference is confined to the Ready/Start routing of startup protocols 0-2 and to the read-only display of the armed choice; it matches docs/P2P_DEFERRED_HOST_START.md (\"Ready / Start: proceed at once\", \"UI keeps its gate for protocol 3\").",
    "Protocol 3 routing is reached through the unchanged isProductionLocalRoom() test and the unchanged beginCampaignLocalHost(); the waiting branch of onCampaignHostReady (generation capture, ui_p2p_initial_handoff, the 180 s limit) follows the new block textually unchanged.",
    "The new code sends only the commands p2p_start_intent, p2p_room, p2p_localhost 1 and (through the existing cancel helper) p2p_cancel_start, built from the same validated map/context strings as before. Its other outward calls are ones the classes already made (Dvar_GetString, the START_MATCH request, SetReadyState through applyRoomReadyState, showMsg); LocalizeUtil.localize is new to LocalMatchControls. No dvar is written.",
    "Observation: a silently revoked launch watch (owner change, changed map/context, untick, leave) cancels the native permission but does not take Ready back; only a failed start does.",
    "Observation: in protocols 0-2 refreshStatus sets mouseEnabled/mouseChildren false on the whole helper on every protocol frame; the protocol 3 branch re-enables only the checkbox. A protocol change during one client run would leave the helper non-interactive; the protocol is fixed per run.",
    "Observation: the captions STARTING HOST... and HOST ERROR are literal English text, not localization keys."
  ],
